  "review_summary": "Question 6 verified leaf-by-leaf against QP PDF pages 14-15 and MS PDF page 11. All 6 leaves thoroughly reviewed for physics correctness, mathematical rigor, syllabus taxonomy alignment, and pedagogical scaffolding. Covers definition of rectification (a.c. to d.c.), contrast between half-wave (removed) and full-wave (reversed) rectification, circuit diagram completion for half-wave rectification with standard diode symbol, identification of capacitor purpose as smoothing, proof of C = 570 μF using E = 0.5 C V^2 and peak voltage 12 V, and exponential discharge calculation yielding R = 43 Ω over a 0.010 s decay from 12 V to 8 V.",
